Hi! This sounds like maybe the BAYAREALIKE model results are being plotted, but are being called BAYAREALIKE+J.  This can happen if some other step of the script is missed or some such. Typically BAYAREALIKE+J looks very similar to DEC+J and DIVALIKE+J.

If you send me the inputs/outputs & script I can take a look, probably on Monday though...
Cheers,
Nick

